{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>You have withheld the purity of it</b> — its sanctuary, which is pure, on the pattern of מקדש ה' כוננו ידיך (the sanctuary of YHWH, your hands established). And a kamatz gadol replaces [what would be] a sheva because of a guttural letter." "And he said מטהרו — because there is no place on earth as pure as it. And the meaning of the vav is that it is the first cause for the building of the sanctuary, for he prepared the silver and the gold." "<b>You have cast down</b> — as in the Targum: ימגר כל מלך (every king shall be cast down)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 89, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:40.298017487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}